#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Some portions generated by Codex.
import pathlib,json
p=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent;s=json.loads((p/'summary.json').read_text());ids=json.loads((p/'source-identities.json').read_text())
a=['# Ordered compact values: actual Workbench results','','## Verdict','','The ordered adapter did not establish an incremental gain on the qualified depth+serializer stack: full completion was 2.12% lower pooled, with mixed paired signs and a descriptive unadjusted 95% reduction interval of -6.70% to +10.19%. First-row latency was 4.88% lower pooled but also inconclusive. The existing qualified stack alone was 14.31% lower completion latency than base in this same matched series (all four pairs favorable, descriptive 95% reduction interval 4.35%–23.25%; derived throughput +16.70%). Its first-row latency was 1.82% slower pooled and inconclusive. Combined versus base was 16.13% lower with all four pairs favorable, but that total must not be credited to the ordered adapter. Ordered-only versus base was inconclusive; no factorial synergy was established. This interaction concerns the entire qualified stack, not independent depth or serializer effects. Do not promote the adapter as a proven incremental performance win.','','The workload is real on-disk LMDB with synthetic RDF data, actual RDF4J Server binary output, actual Workbench Java decoding and NDJSON serialization, and a Node streaming client. It excludes browser rendering, concurrent QPS, remote-network effects and the historical wide eight-million-row fixture.','','## Immutable arms','']
for x in ids:a.append(f'- **{x}**: `{ids[x]}`.')
a+=['','All arms use the same reconstructed frozen server/dependency stack, pinned PR #6440 writer, compact identity mapping, memo/IR flags and full six-slot 100,000-row response. Each ordered layer contains only nine classes in QueryEvaluator, TupleResultBuilder and WorkbenchPageResultWriter families. Both pristine nine-class baselines recompiled byte-identical to their actual frozen base/stack runtime. The ordered-only source does not include typed serialization; combined retains it. Read-resource holder, cancellation changes, initializer null-slot restoration and the grouped test-only observer are excluded. The archive branch is not a runtime identity.','','## Protocol and qualification','','One prespecified four-block Latin square, four independent fresh JVMs per arm. Each fork completed 60 warmups and 30 measured sequential queries: 1,440 requests total, 480 measured. Every request passed compiled IR, memo, binary MIME, row count, no-spill, ledger cleanup and class-origin checks. Four separate untimed qualification queries validated every term, uniqueness and dual checksums. All samples were retained; no trimming or additional clean round. Startup and client setup are outside POST-to-EOF latency.','','Correctness: 1,574 Workbench module tests passed; isolated ordered-only 126 and combined 128 passed with hardened expected-count and container checks. Initial missing spring-test zero-test launcher runs were failures, retained and fixed before qualification. Exact-byte, subclass/mock fallback, lookup/prepacking order, no retention and streaming/error behavior were independently reviewed. This is not a whole-repository pass.','','## Clean means','','| Arm | EOF ms | First row ms | Derived rows/s | Fork EOF range ms |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for x in ids:
 v=s['arms'][x];m=v['means'];lo,hi=v['forkRangeEofMs'];a.append(f"| {x} | {m['eofMs']:.3f} | {m['firstRowMs']:.3f} | {100000000/m['eofMs']:.0f} | {lo:.3f}–{hi:.3f} |")
a+=['','Rows/s is the reciprocal of sequential full-response latency, not concurrent serving capacity.','','| Contrast | EOF reduction % | Paired reductions % | Descriptive 95% interval % |','|---|---:|---|---|']
for k,v in s['contrasts'].items():
 q=v['eofMs'];a.append(f"| {k} | {q['latencyReductionPercent']:.3f} | {', '.join(f'{z:+.2f}' for z in q['pairedReductionPercent'])} | {q['descriptive95ReductionInterval'][0]:+.2f} to {q['descriptive95ReductionInterval'][1]:+.2f} |")
v=s['interaction']['eofMs'];a += ['',f"Factorial geometric interaction ratio: **{v['geometricInteractionRatio']:.3f}**, descriptive 95% interval **{v['descriptive95RatioInterval'][0]:.3f}–{v['descriptive95RatioInterval'][1]:.3f}**. Values below one suggest supermultiplicative latency reduction, but this wide interval crosses one. Intervals use paired log fork means and t with three degrees of freedom; they are unadjusted for multiple contrasts and do not establish equivalence.",'','## All independent fork means','','| Fork | Arm | EOF ms | First row ms |','|---|---|---:|---:|']
for f in s['forks']:a.append(f"| {f['name']} | {f['arm']} | {f['means']['eofMs']:.3f} | {f['means']['firstRowMs']:.3f} |")
a+=['','## Convergence and limitations','','| Arm | First measured third ms | Middle third ms | Last third ms |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
for x,v in s['arms'].items():a.append('| '+x+' | '+' | '.join(f'{z:.3f}' for z in v['measuredThirdMeanEofMs'])+' |')
a+=['','Longer fixed warmup does not automatically prove convergence; measured thirds above retain evidence of drift or variation. We retain the full prespecified interval rather than select its faster tail. Four forks per arm constrain precision; request samples within a fork are not independent replications. Earlier embedded depth gains do not establish a gain through this HTTP pipeline.','','Whole-JVM GC logs include startup/warmup, not query-attributed pauses. Heap-used before/after snapshots are not allocation or retained heap. RSS was not collected; no memory-capacity conclusion follows. The browser remains unmeasured following the prior policy-blocked launch; no retry or bypass occurred.','','## Evidence','','`summary.json` retains every fork and index, GC summaries, first application-query values and all contrasts. `runs/matched-*` retain raw request metrics, commands and logs. `protocol.json`, source IDs, class manifests and the frozen common manifests establish provenance. Separate JFR results are reported in `HTTP-PROFILES.md`, never pooled into the clean timing population.','']
(p/'RESULTS.md').write_text('\n'.join(a))
with (p/'RESULTS.md').open('a') as f:
 f.write('\n## First-row contrasts\n\nPositive reductions mean lower latency. These are separate from full completion; all intervals remain descriptive and unadjusted.\n\n| Contrast | Reduction % | Paired reductions % | 95% interval % |\n|---|---:|---|---|\n')
 for name in ['both-versus-stack','ordered-versus-base','stack-versus-base','both-versus-base']:
  q=s['contrasts'][name]['firstRowMs'];f.write(f"| {name} | {q['latencyReductionPercent']:.2f} | {', '.join(f'{x:+.2f}' for x in q['pairedReductionPercent'])} | {q['descriptive95ReductionInterval'][0]:+.2f} to {q['descriptive95ReductionInterval'][1]:+.2f} |\n")
 f.write('\n## Published evidence packaging\n\n`evidence/index.json` and ordered pool chunks reconstruct every textual run artifact losslessly. Concatenate pool lines by index, or for compactJsonFrom log entries compact the reconstructed JSON outside quoted strings and append a newline. All exact-byte SHA-256 round trips are verified by package-evidence.py. Originals remain local; raw JFR and huge full-stack exports are excluded, compact summaries included.\n')
